            'liq.ui.pintle_post_diameter': 'Pintle Post Diameter D_p',
            'liq.ui.pintle_post_diameter_tip': 'Outer diameter of the pintle post at its tip (D_p, mm); the fuel tip holes are drilled into it and the oxidizer flows through the annulus around it. With the annulus area fixed by the oxidizer circuit, D_p sets the annular gap t, and through the blockage factor the tip-hole count. Must be a finite positive length; the annulus bore D_p + 2t must fit inside the chamber. Empty: sized from the oxidizer flow with the annulus rule t = 0.05·D_p (HRMA choice, no literature value).',
            'liq.ui.pintle_annular_gap': 'Oxidizer Annular Gap t',
            'liq.ui.pintle_annular_gap_tip': 'Radial gap of the oxidizer annulus around the pintle post (t, mm). The annulus area pi·(D_p + t)·t must equal the oxidizer circuit flow area: given alone, D_p is solved from it; given with D_p, the two must agree within 5% (HRMA tolerance) or the design is rejected with the mismatch. Empty: solved from the oxidizer flow area.',
            'liq.ui.pintle_fuel_hole_count': 'Fuel Tip Hole Count n',
            'liq.ui.pintle_fuel_hole_count_tip': 'Number of radial fuel holes in the single row on the pintle tip (whole number ≥ 1). The holes carry the fuel circuit flow area n·pi·d²/4, so the hole diameter follows from n. Empty: from the blockage factor n·d/(pi·D_p) = 0.58 (HRMA choice, no literature value).',
            'liq.ui.pintle_fuel_hole_diameter': 'Fuel Tip Hole Diameter d',
            'liq.ui.pintle_fuel_hole_diameter_tip': 'Diameter of each radial fuel tip hole (d, mm). Given alone, the hole count is the nearest whole number for this diameter and the published diameter is the one that delivers the fuel circuit area exactly with that count; a plan more than 5% off (also with a given count) is rejected with the nearest valid plans. Empty: solved from the fuel flow area.',
            'liq.ui.pintle_skip_distance': 'Skip Distance L_s',
            'liq.ui.pintle_skip_distance_tip': 'Axial distance from the annulus exit (injector face) to the axis of the tip-hole row (L_s, mm; definition Dressler & Bauer, AIAA 2000-3871). Geometry and CAD only: no performance model uses it. Must be shorter than the chamber. Empty: L_s = D_p (HRMA choice, no literature value).',
            'liq.ui.ph_solver_sizes': 'solver sizes',
            'liq.ui.ph_ls_equals_dp': 'L_s = D_p if empty',
            'liq.ui.injector_material': 'Injector Plate Material',
            'liq.ui.injector_material_tip': 'Material of the injector face plate. Used only in the injector plate structural check: a clamped circular plate (Roark Table 11.2, case 10b) of the chamber diameter under the injector pressure drop, with ASME PG-52 ligament efficiency from the fuel + oxidizer hole plan (all holes at the larger diameter, conservative). It gives the plate thickness that meets the Structural Safety Factor from the room-temperature yield strength; the page has no plate-thickness input. Not run for pintle, coaxial and swirl elements (no drilled-hole plan; the result says why). Empty: the check is not run. An unknown name is rejected.',
            'liq.ui.injector_material_not_selected': 'Not selected (plate check not run)',
