            'liq.ui.feed_pressure_note_pressure_fed': 'Pressure-fed: this is the tank pressure. The solver sizes the propellant tanks and the feed-line and valve pressure budget from it and checks it against the pressure the chamber needs (tank pressure margin).',
            'liq.ui.feed_pressure_note_turbopump': 'Turbopump cycle: this value is only a target pump discharge pressure. The solver computes the discharge pressure it needs and warns if this value is lower; the tanks are pressurised for pump NPSH only.',
            'liq.ui.pressure_drop_across_injector_as_percentage': 'Absolute pressure drop across the injector, in bar. Leave it EMPTY and HRMA sets the drop as chamber pressure x a dP/Pc factor of the injector type (impinging 0.22, coaxial 0.18, showerhead 0.28, pintle 0.15, other types 0.20); the result labels it "NASA SP-8089 dP/Pc ratio for the element type". A number you type is used as bar and labelled "user input (injector pressure drop)". Accepted 0.2-200 bar: a value outside that band is refused by name and no design is published. A drop with dP/Pc outside 0.05-0.40 is calculated but warned (SP-8089 guideline). A larger drop improves mixing and stability but raises the required feed pressure.',
            'liq.ui.pressure_fed': 'Pressure-Fed',
            'liq.ui.pressure_of_hot_gas_entering_turbine': 'Turbine inlet pressure (bar), turbopump cycles only. When the turbine expansion ratio is also entered, the solver uses that ratio and only compares this value with the inlet pressure its cycle balance needs (a warning names both). Leave the expansion ratio empty and the ratio is solved from this pressure. Accepted 1-1000 bar.',
