            'solid.ui.export_formats': 'Export formats:',
            'solid.ui.factor_of_safety_for_case_design': 'Factor of safety for case design. Typical values: 2-4. Higher values provide more safety margin but increase case weight. Required by safety codes for amateur rocketry.',
            'solid.ui.family': 'Family',
            'solid.ui.family_help': 'Display filter for the propellant catalogue table below: shows only the chosen family. It does not change the selected propellant or any calculation.',
            'solid.ui.fillet_radius': 'Fillet Radius',
            'solid.ui.fills_a_and_n_from_the': 'Burn-rate law of the selected propellant. KNDX/KNSB: the piecewise regime table (Nakka 1999/2001 fits) is read at the instantaneous chamber pressure, and a, n show the regime at the current design pressure. Custom: the single a-n pair in the boxes below is used (for a propellant without a regime table this is its catalogue pair). The preset follows the "Propellant (catalogue record)" selector; choosing another propellant\'s preset switches the selector to it, so a regime table can never belong to a different propellant (the solver rejects such a mix). Editing a or n manually switches to Custom.',
            'solid.ui.filter_cutoff_frequency': 'Filter Cutoff Frequency',
