            'solid.ui.flow_discharge_coefficient_for_mass_flow': 'Flow discharge coefficient for mass flow through nozzle throat. Accounts for viscous effects and flow non-uniformities. Typical values: 0.97-0.99.',
            'solid.ui.formulas': 'Formulas',
            'solid.ui.free_volume_inside_the_motor_case': 'Your stated free volume inside the case (case bore minus propellant), in litres. The solver derives this volume from the geometry and uses its own value; the number you type is only compared with it and a named warning appears when they disagree (measured: changing it changes only the warnings, not thrust, pressure or burn time). Blank (default): nothing is sent and no comparison is made. Accepted range 0.001-100000 L.',
            'solid.ui.front_face': 'Front Face',
            'solid.ui.fuel': 'Fuel',
            'solid.ui.grain_support': 'Grain Support',
            'solid.ui.grain_support_case_bonded': 'Case-bonded',
            'solid.ui.grain_support_cartridge_loaded': 'Cartridge-loaded (free-standing)',
            'solid.ui.grain_support_help': 'How the grain is held in the case. Case-bonded: cast and cured inside the case and bonded to its liner; the case restrains the cure and cool-down shrinkage, so the bore carries that thermal strain on top of the pressure strain. Cartridge-loaded: cast in a mold or liner outside the case and inserted, bonded at most at its ends (NASA SP-8073); no shrinkage strain is restrained, and the pressure strain is computed with the case supporting the grain (snug fit, upper bound). Changes only the grain structural results (bore strain, strain safety factor, crack risk), not the ballistics. If the field is not sent, case-bonded is used and declared in the result.',
            'solid.ui.geometric_configuration_of_the_solid_propellant': 'Geometric configuration of the solid propellant grain. BATES: cylinder with a central core port. Star: star-shaped core port. Finocyl: core port with fins for a larger burning surface. Wagon Wheel: multiple core ports. End Burner: no core port, burns from one end only. The thrust profile is NOT fixed by the shape alone (it also depends on the inhibitor layout and the port-to-throat ratio); this run\u0027s profile is classified by the solver and printed under \u0022Thrust Curve\u0022.',
            'solid.ui.grain_geometry': 'Grain geometry:',
            'solid.ui.grain_length': 'Grain Length',
            'solid.ui.grain_to_grain_gap': 'Grain-to-Grain Gap',
            'solid.ui.grain_type': 'Grain Type',
            'solid.ui.gray_components': 'Gray components:',
            'solid.ui.half_angle_of_convergent_section_approaching': 'Half-angle of convergent section approaching the throat. Typical values: 20-45°. Affects flow uniformity and pressure losses in subsonic region.',
            'solid.ui.half_angle_of_divergent_section_after': 'Half-angle of divergent section after the throat. Typical values: 12-18°. Larger angles cause flow separation, smaller angles increase nozzle length and weight.',
            'solid.ui.heat_of_combustion_hc': 'Heat of Combustion ΔHc',
            'solid.ui.home': 'Home',
            'solid.ui.how_to_use': 'How to use:',
            'solid.ui.humidity': 'Humidity',
            'solid.ui.hybrid': 'Hybrid',
            'solid.ui.ignition_delay': 'Ignition Delay',
            'solid.ui.ignition_transient_steady_state_tail_off': 'Ignition transient, steady-state, tail-off regions',
            'solid.ui.in_millimetres_mm': 'In millimetres (mm)',
            'solid.ui.inhibitor_coating': 'Inhibitor Coating',
            'solid.ui.initial_chamber_temperature_before_ignition_affe': 'Grain (propellant conditioning) temperature T0 at ignition, in K - not the chamber gas temperature. The burn rate is shifted with the exponential law a_T = a·exp(σp·(T0 − T_ref)) (σp: Temperature Coefficient field, T_ref: the record reference temperature), so chamber pressure, thrust, burn time and Isp change with it (measured on the KNDX example: +20 K changes all four). It also anchors the cold/hot-day sensitivity table. Blank: T0 = T_ref (no shift). Accepted range 200-350 K.',
            'solid.ui.initial_diameter_of_the_central_core': 'Initial diameter of the central core hole (port diameter). Determines initial burning surface area and thrust profile. Measured in this solver for a BATES grain with burning ends (10-60 mm cores): the end plateau is below the start plateau at every core (end/start 0.09-0.49) and a larger core falls off less, but the trend is not monotonic (0.11 at 10 mm, 0.09 at 15 mm, 0.21 at 30 mm, 0.49 at 60 mm). At 10 mm the solver classifies the curve as Progressive-Regressive (thrust rises first, then falls), so this is not a single class over the whole core range. The published shape class comes from thrust_profile_analysis.thrust_curve_type in the result, not from this hint.',
            'solid.ui.initial_temperature': 'Initial Temperature',
            'solid.ui.initial_wet_mass_kg': 'Initial (Wet) Mass (kg)',
            'solid.ui.initial_wet_mass_kg_help': 'Vehicle mass at lift-off (kg), sent as initial_mass to /api/trajectory-analysis. After a motor calculation it is filled with the solver\'s total mass (design_summary.masses.total_mass_kg) unless you typed a value. Initial − final mass must match the propellant the motor burns (within the endpoint tolerance), otherwise no trajectory is computed and both masses are named. Empty or not a number: the field is not sent and the trajectory endpoint refuses the run, naming the field (no value is assumed).',
            'solid.ui.inputs': 'Inputs:',
            'solid.ui.insulation_mass': 'Insulation Mass',
            'solid.ui.insulation_thickness': 'Insulation Thickness',
            'solid.ui.interactive_3d_cad_model_of_solid': 'Interactive 3D CAD model of solid rocket motor assembly',
            'solid.ui.interactive_controls': 'Interactive controls:',
            'solid.ui.internal_diameter_of_the_motor_casing': 'Case inner diameter in mm - the bore that holds the grain, liner and insulation (the grain outer diameter is its own field). It sizes the case wall, the case mass and the burst margin. Blank: derived as grain outer diameter + 2·(liner + insulation) and shown after Calculate. A value below that minimum is rejected with the minimum named; the case is never enlarged silently. Accepted range 10-5000 mm.',
            'solid.ui.keep_my_edits': 'Keep my edits',
            'solid.ui.kinetic_efficiency': 'Kinetic Efficiency',
            'solid.ui.kndx_kno3_dextrose_65_35_nakka': 'KNDX — KNO3/Dextrose 65/35 (Nakka fit)',
            'solid.ui.knsb_kno3_sorbitol_65_35_nakka': 'KNSB — KNO3/Sorbitol 65/35 (Nakka fit)',
            'solid.ui.liner_density': 'Liner Density',
            'solid.ui.liner_thickness': 'Liner Thickness',
