            'solid.ui.loading_catalogue': 'Loading catalogue...',
            'solid.ui.low_pass_filter_cutoff_frequency_for': 'Low-pass filter cutoff frequency for noise reduction. Should be high enough to preserve real data but low enough to remove noise. Typically 50-200 Hz for motor testing.',
            'solid.ui.manual_edits_are_protected': 'Manual edits are protected:',
            'solid.ui.mass_of_electronic_systems_including_flight': 'Mass of electronic systems including flight computer, sensors, telemetry, and recovery systems. Not part of motor but affects overall vehicle performance.',
            'solid.ui.mass_of_motor_casing_including_forward': 'Mass of motor casing including forward and aft closures. Depends on material, pressure rating, and safety factor. Major component of dry mass.',
            'solid.ui.mass_of_nozzle_assembly_including_throat': 'Mass of nozzle assembly including throat insert, exit cone, and mounting hardware. Varies with nozzle material and size.',
            'solid.ui.mass_of_thermal_insulation_materials_including': 'Mass of thermal insulation materials including liner, inhibitor coatings, and heat barriers. Protects case from high temperatures.',
            'solid.ui.masses_and_burn_time_are_pre': 'Masses and burn time are pre-filled from the current design and remain editable',
            'solid.ui.material_for_motor_casing_construction_steel': 'Material of the motor case. The case wall is sized against hoop stress with this material\'s yield strength (see the yield source below), the case and closure mass come from its density, and the case thermal verdict compares the computed case wall temperature with its service temperature limit (shown below the selection; where no limit is on record the verdict is not evaluated). Options come from the server material records; a name the server cannot resolve is rejected.',
            'solid.ui.material_for_nozzle_construction_graphite_good': 'Material of the nozzle throat insert. The throat thermal check compares the adiabatic wall temperature at the throat (uncooled throat, worst case T_wall → T_aw) with the allowable temperature of this material record; above it the verdict is EXCEEDS_ALLOWABLE (critical warning). Throat erosion uses a published coefficient band only where one exists (shown below); otherwise a rigid throat is assumed and stated. Options come from the server material records; a name the server cannot resolve is rejected (no verdict is derived from another material). Phenolic is not offered: there is no sourced throat record and no ablation model.',
            'solid.ui.material_specific_coefficient_in_burn_rate': 'Burn-rate coefficient a of r [m/s] = a × (P [bar])^n. With the Burn Rate Preset on a propellant\'s regime table (KNDX, KNSB) the solver reads the table at the instantaneous pressure and this box only shows the coefficient of the current regime; with Custom it is the a used in every step. Picking a catalogue record fills it (see the catalogue row for each propellant\'s value); typing here switches the preset to Custom. Blank: the selected record\'s a is used.',
            'solid.ui.max_service_temp_k': 'Max service temp. (K)',
            'solid.ui.maximum_force_point_design_critical_point': 'Maximum force point (design critical point)',
            'solid.ui.maximum_operating_pressure_for_safety_analysis': 'Maximum operating pressure for safety analysis',
            'solid.ui.maximum_pressure_measurement_range_of_pressure': 'Maximum pressure measurement range of pressure transducer. Should be 1.5-2x expected maximum pressure for accuracy and safety. Typical range: 5-15 MPa for amateur motors.',
            'solid.ui.maximum_theoretical_combustion_temperature_apcp': 'Adiabatic flame (chamber) temperature T_c in K. It sets the gas enthalpy behind c* and Isp and the throat heat flux. "Catalogue record" mode: shows the selected record\'s value at one pressure (see the catalogue row) and is not sent; the value the solver used (NASA CEA at the motor chamber pressure) appears below after Calculate. "My values" mode: this number is sent and used. Accepted range 1000-4500 K.',
            'solid.ui.maximum_thrust_measurement_capacity_of_load': 'Maximum thrust measurement capacity of load cell. Should be 1.5-2x expected maximum thrust for accuracy. Includes safety margin for unexpected over-pressure events.',
            'solid.ui.minimum_flow_area_and_diverging_cone': 'Minimum flow area and diverging cone',
            'solid.ui.minimum_thickness_of_propellant_that_burns': 'Derived output, read-only: the propellant web implied by the grain geometry ((outer − core)/2), filled after Calculate. When the outer surface burns as well the web is consumed from both faces, so the thickness actually burnt is half of it (see web_burnout_mm). Typing here changes no result.',
            'solid.ui.molecular_weight_m': 'Molecular Weight M',
            'solid.ui.monte_carlo_analysis_manufacturing_tolerances': 'Monte Carlo Analysis (Manufacturing Tolerances)',
            'solid.ui.motor_analysis_solid_propellant': 'MOTOR ANALYSIS - Solid Propellant',
