            'solid.ui.radius_of_star_points_from_center': 'Radius of star points from center. Determines burning surface area and progressive characteristics.',
            'solid.ui.randomly_samples_the_manufacturing_tolerances_bu': 'Randomly samples the manufacturing tolerances (burn-rate coefficient a, exponent n, density, C*) and derives the statistical distribution of motor performance.',
            'solid.ui.range_that_contains_90_of_the': 'Range that contains 90% of the runs',
            'solid.ui.rate_of_throat_diameter_increase_due': 'Throat erosion reference rate a_ref in mm/s at the erosion law reference pressure (the empirical model scales it to the chamber pressure; the reference pressure is named in the erosion result). A value above 0 is sent and the solver erodes the throat with it during the burn; 0 means no erosion (rigid throat by choice). Blank (default): the solver keeps a rigid throat and, for a nozzle material with a published band (graphite), estimates the erosion and prints the rate it found at the chamber pressure in the warnings; for a material without a published band no erosion number is published. There is no single typical value - see the nozzle material properties line. Accepted range 0-5 mm/s.',
            'solid.ui.ratio_of_exit_area_to_throat': 'Ratio of exit area to throat area (Ae/At). Automatically calculated from diameters. Higher ratios provide better performance at altitude but risk flow separation at sea level.',
            'solid.ui.ratio_of_specific_heats_cp_cv': 'Ratio of specific heats γ = Cp/Cv of the chamber gas. It enters c* and the nozzle expansion (exit pressure, thrust coefficient). "Catalogue record" mode: shows the selected record\'s value at one pressure and is not sent; the solver\'s value (NASA CEA at the motor chamber pressure, shifting equilibrium) appears below after Calculate. "My values" mode: this number is sent and used. Accepted range 1.05-1.5.',
            'solid.ui.rear_face': 'Rear Face',
