            'solid.ui.temperature_coefficient': 'Temperature Coefficient σ',
            'solid.ui.temperature_sensitivity_coefficient_for_burn_rat': 'Temperature sensitivity σp of the burn rate (1/K). The solver uses the exponential law a_T = a·exp(σp·(T0 − T_ref)), where T0 is the grain temperature (Initial Temperature field) and T_ref the record reference temperature; it shifts the burn rate, so chamber pressure, thrust and burn time change when T0 ≠ T_ref. It also sets the cold/hot-day sensitivity table. Source selector: "Catalogue" uses the propellant record value (read-only box, filled after Calculate); "My value" sends this number. Blank in "My value" mode: nothing is sent and the catalogue value is used. Accepted range 0-0.02 1/K.',
            'solid.ui.test_altitude': 'Test Altitude',
            'solid.ui.theoretical_performance_parameter_independent_of': 'Theoretical characteristic velocity c* in m/s, before the combustion efficiency. It sizes the throat (A_t = ṁ·c*/Pc) and the thrust. "Catalogue record" mode: shows the selected record\'s value at one pressure (see the catalogue row) and is not sent; the solver\'s value (NASA CEA at the motor chamber pressure) appears below after Calculate. "My values" mode: this number is sent and replaces the thermochemistry (NASA CEA is not applied). "Calculate" computes c* from γ, T_c and M (Sutton & Biblarz Eq. 3-32) and switches the source to "My values". Accepted range 700-2500 m/s; outside it the value is ignored with a warning.',
            'solid.ui.thickness_of_each_fin_slot_affects': 'Thickness of each fin slot. Affects burning surface area and grain structural integrity.',
